From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:03:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] manager: Korea's alert names, and "Public Safety Alert"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Korean alerts came titled "Public Savety Alert". Fix the spelling, and
with a Korean network name the alerts as Android does there
(CellBroadcastReceiver res/values-mcc450): Extreme Emergency Alert
(위급재난문자), Emergency Alert (긴급재난문자), Public Safety Alert
(안전안내문자), Amber Alert (실종경보문자).

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/cbd-manager.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cbd-manager.c b/src/cbd-manager.c
index 3fb4082..e865b6f 100644
--- a/src/cbd-manager.c
+++ b/src/cbd-manager.c
@@ -351,8 +351,26 @@ load_from_db (CbdManager *self)
 
 
 static const char *
-severity_to_string (LcbSeverityLevel level)
+severity_to_string (LcbSeverityLevel level, const char *country)
 {
+  /* Korea names its alerts by its own scheme (위급재난문자, 긴급재난문자, 안전안내문자,
+   * 실종경보문자); these are the English names Android uses there
+   * (CellBroadcastReceiver res/values-mcc450/strings.xml). */
+  if (country && !g_ascii_strcasecmp (country, "kr")) {
+    switch (level) {
+    case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_PRESIDENTIAL:
+      return "Extreme Emergency Alert";
+    case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_EXTREME:
+      return "Emergency Alert";
+    case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_PUBLIC_SAFETY:
+      return "Public Safety Alert";
+    case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_AMBER:
+      return "Amber Alert";
+    default:
+      break;
+    }
+  }
+
   switch (level) {
   case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_PRESIDENTIAL:
     return "Nation Wide Alert";
@@ -361,7 +379,7 @@ severity_to_string (LcbSeverityLevel level)
   case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_SEVERE:
     return "Severe Danger Alert";
   case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_PUBLIC_SAFETY:
-    return "Public Savety Alert";
+    return "Public Safety Alert";
   case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_AMBER:
     return "Amber Alert";
   case LCB_SEVERITY_LEVEL_TEST:
@@ -530,7 +548,7 @@ on_new_cbm (CbdMmManager *mm_manager,
   channel_manager = cbd_mm_manager_get_channel_manager (mm_manager);
   severity = cbd_channel_manager_lookup_level (channel_manager, channel);
 
-  severity_subject = severity_to_string (severity);
+  severity_subject = severity_to_string (severity, cbd_channel_manager_get_country (channel_manager));
   msg = cbd_message_new (text,
                          channel,
                          msg_code,
-- 
